# Check the working tree before executing anything

Before edits, installs, merges, pulls, commits, pushes, deploys, or other mutating commands, inspect the repo. Do not assume the previous chat’s branch is still the right place to work.

## Required checks (read-only first)

Run together:

1. `git status` — clean vs dirty, merge/rebase in progress, untracked files
2. `git branch --show-current` — never treat `develop`/`main` as a feature branch
3. Tracking vs remote — `git status` “ahead/behind”; fetch if you will merge or branch

Also confirm:

- Open PR for this branch: `gh pr view --json state,mergedAt,url` (or `gh pr list --head <branch>`)
- If the user mentions a PR number, check that PR **before** pulling or merging

## Stop or redirect when

| State | Action |
|-------|--------|
| Dirty tree unrelated to the request | Do not mix work; stash/leave those files alone |
| Merge/rebase conflict in progress | Finish or abort that first; do not start a new task on top |
| On `develop` or `main` | Branch off up-to-date `develop` (`feature/` / `fix/` / `chore/`) before editing |
| Feature branch whose PR is already **MERGED** | Switch to up-to-date `develop`; do not `git pull origin develop` into the dead branch |
| Requested work already on `develop` | Do not re-implement; say so |
| Behind `origin/develop` and starting new work | Fast-forward/checkout `develop`, then new branch |

## Do not

- Pull `develop` into a merged feature branch to “sync”
- Commit/push/PR until the checks above say this branch is the right target
- Skip these checks because the last turn already ran git (re-check; state changes)

## Example

User pastes a merge conflict from `git pull origin develop` on `feature/openai-…`:

1. Check `git status` + `gh pr view 124` → PR **MERGED**
2. Tell the user the work is already on `develop`
3. Do not continue implementing or merging into that feature branch
